    "created_at": "2026-01-06T23:31:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T23:32:02Z",
    "body": "I think the use case here is that some component A which wraps each slotted element in a wrapper element in its shadow tree has another component B, which pulls in the slotted content for A's slot via its own slot, as its parent. So the tree looks like this:\n```\nB -- ShadowRoot\n|    + -- A -- ShadowRoot\n|         |    + -- wrapper 1\n|         |    |    + -- slot 1 (in A's shadow tree)\n|         |    |\n|         |    + -- wrapper 2\n|         |    |    + -- slot 2 (in A's shadow tree)\n|         |    |\n|         |    ...\n|         |\n|         + slot X (in B's shadow tree)\n|\n+ -- div\n|    + ...\n|    |\n|    ...\n|\n+ -- div\n     + ...\n     |\n     ...\n```\n\nIn this scenario, conceptually, each element assigned to \"slot X\" wants to be wrapped in its own wrapper element in A's shadow tree but this is not possible today because you can't selectively assign a node assigned to a slotted slot.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
