    "created_at": "2026-01-07T14:02:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T15:06:17Z",
    "body": "If I am reading correctly, what @rniwa explained is what I am after.\n\nIf I author reusable component \"A\" that wraps each element using manual slot assignment, I want to also be able to author component \"B\" that populates A using \"slot X\", where each element assigned to \"slot X\" should get it's own wrapper in A's shadow tree.\n\nMy proposed solution is to provide a mechanism for CE's to forward nodes assigned to a slot into separate slots by loosening restrictions on HTMLSlotElement.assign().\n\nWhile this would require allowing nodes to be assigned to more than one slot, if a CE can only forward nodes assigned to a slot when that slot is one of its children, the practical effect is that a given node is still rendered in at most one location, so long as the CE is prevented from forwarding a node to more than one slot.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
